   "id": "y93-crawford-mvp",
   "kind": "feature",
   "headline": "The Doctor Throws 64 Touchdown Passes and Wins a Fourth MVP",
   "dek": "Bones Crawford played all 20 games, completed 281 of 317 passes and won his fifth ring, every one of them in Philadelphia.",
   "body": [
    "A year after injury cost him 4 games, Bones Crawford, \"The Doctor\", was on the field for all 20 of Philadelphia's games. He threw for 4,936 yards and 64 touchdowns with 11 interceptions, 3.2 touchdown passes a game, and completed 281 of his 317 attempts.",
    "The league named him Most Valuable Player for the 4th time. Nobody threw more touchdown passes; Tim Sweeney of the Texans was next with 45. Crawford's overall rose from 80 to 86, his Career Legacy from 7,332 to 8,158, and his card's value by 142.6%.",
    "He is 28 and has 5 rings, all won with the Eagles. He had help: tight end Jacob Proise caught 46 passes for 837 yards, and Akiem Brock made 51 blocks, more than any other lineman in the league, as his overall climbed to 94."
