   "kind": "rivalry",
   "headline": "Three Tries, Three Losses: Ty Lock's Giants Still Cannot Beat Philadelphia",
   "dek": "New York lost 30-22, 24-23 and 38-28 to the Eagles and has now lost all 13 meetings since Y88. Washington was swept again.",
   "body": [
    "Ty Lock won two rings with Skura's Jets, in Y80 and Y82, with Ryland Maxwell in the same backfield. A trade sent him to the Giants before Y83, and he has been on the other side ever since. In Y93 he faced his old coach three times.",
    "New York lost 30-22 in Philadelphia in week 15. In week 18 the Giants came within a point at home, losing 24-23, the narrowest of the Eagles' 20 wins. They met again in the conference final and lost 38-28. Lock, 37, threw for 3,550 yards and 26 touchdowns with 3 interceptions, and Niles Canaday, 23, ran for 1,898 yards and 40 touchdowns, the most in the league. Since Y88 the Eagles are 13-0 against the Giants.",
    "The Commanders, who had split the series for three straight seasons before Y92, were swept for the second year running, 48-22 in Philadelphia and 40-28 in Washington. The series since Y88 now stands at 7-4-1."
